A||||2||yobtah||Help Identifying A/C System "High" and "Low" Sides||||1||
Z||000000||yobtah||08-11-2000||06:28 PM||||I'm thinking about converting my A/C system to r134a.  Before I do it, I want to be sure I know which valve is for the "high side" of the system.  I have an '87 SE V6.  In the front compartment, there's a large silver cannister (the accumulator/condensor, I think) with a valve on it.  There's also a valve on the line connected to the bottom driver's side of the same cannister.  I'm assuming one valve corresponds to the "high side" and the other to the "low side."  Can anyone help me identify the valves?  Thanks for any info!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||08-11-2000||07:27 PM||||The valve on the cannister is the low. Be sure to read all the posts on the change over ||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||08-12-2000||09:02 AM||||They're sized differently. When you put on the adapter fittings for the R134, the "high" will only fit on the high, and vice versa.<P>So there's no way you can screw it up.||||reg||1
